"To find the positive difference between \\(120\\%\\) of 30 and \\(130\\%\\) of 20, we first need to calculate each value separately.\n\n1. Calculate \\(120\\%\\) of 30:\n\\[\n120\\% \\text{ of } 30 = 1.20 \\times 30 = 36\n\\]\n\n2. Calculate \\(130\\%\\) of 20:\n\\[\n130\\% \\text{ of } 20 = 1.30 \\times 20 = 26\n\\]\n\n3. Find the positive difference between the two values:\n\\[\n\\text{Positive difference} = |36 - 26| = |10| = 10\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the positive difference between \\(120\\%\\) of 30 and \\(130\\%\\) of 20 is \\(\\boxed{10}\\)."
